For comparison, four B300 with networking are about {{ usd(4 * G_HW.cost.purchase_usd_per_gpu, -3) }}
(reseller range {{ usd(4 * 56000, -3) }} to {{ usd(4 * 76000, -3) }}; b300-price).

Memory is repairable with spare rows. Thus only the {{ pct(1 - S.area.repairable_share) }} of an MDS-1 die
that is logic must be defect-free. The storage of a fixed-weight die has no spares.

These figures do not include vendor margin, spares, the yield of tile assembly, or software and
bring-up. GPUs are at street price, which includes all of them.

We spread the design cost over the systems that a token demand needs (NRE of {{ usd(S_HW.cost.nre_usd / 1e6, 0) }}M; assumption, swept {{ usd(30) }}M to {{ usd(436) }}M).
